{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "7ed6e42b-a966-8db7-93bc-946b1b32caae",
  "created_at": "2026-01-21T13:55:14-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Luis Salazar",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Janet Whitcomb",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:51:19-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Finance Department, Janet Whitcomb speaking. How may I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:51:23-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, good afternoon. My name is Luis Salazar. I'm calling about my mother's property tax, she's at 286 Malbone Road, up the North End. Um, I only have one bar of service in this room, so if I fade out, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:51:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood, Mr. Salazar. I'll speak clearly. Is your mother's account in her name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:51:44-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it's in her name. I'm her son, I handle her mail now. She got a bill, and it says the installment is due, and I don't, I'm not sure I understand how much of it we have to pay right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:51:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The bill should show the amount due for the current installment. Is that the figure you're looking at?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:52:06-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, there's a big number at the top, and then a smaller one lower down. The big one is the whole year, I think. Or is it the half year? Anyway, can I pay part of it? Like, a partial payment, is that allowed, or does it have to be the whole thing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:52:25-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The city does accept payments toward a balance, but any unpaid portion of the installment after the due date would be treated as late. I'd recommend paying the full installment amount if you can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:52:37-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So partial, it takes it, but it's still late on the rest. Okay. Got it. I think."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:52:44-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:52:46-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Now, my mother's over seventy-five, and somebody at the, the old senior center, well, it's not the senior center anymore, the community center, said there's an exemption she might get. Is there a form for that? What's the form number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:53:00-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are exemption applications available through the Assessor's office. I don't have a form number in front of me that I can give you with confidence. I can transfer you to the Assessor, or take your name and have them call you back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:53:15-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, the Assessor. Is that, that's the same office as the, the old tax office, by the, what was it, by the old, never mind. Yes, transfer is fine. Actually wait, first, one more thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:53:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:53:30-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I work until late, I mean I'm over at her house tonight and I won't get to City Hall before it closes. There's a box, a drop box? If I put the check in the box tonight, does that count as on time? The due date is, um, I think it's tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:53:48-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there is a payment drop box at City Hall. Payments placed in the box are collected the next business day. Please check the due date printed on your bill, and make sure the check is made out correctly with the account number on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:04-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So tonight in the box, it counts for tomorrow's date, even though you pick it up after."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:11-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I would say the box is meant for exactly that purpose, but the due date on your bill is what governs. If it says tomorrow, tonight's drop is the safe way to get it there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:24-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And the account number, that's the, it's on the top right of the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:30-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It should be labeled on the stub, the portion you tear off and send back. Write it on the memo line of the check as well."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:40-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The stub. Okay, I see a stub. [line breaks up] sorry, did you say memo line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the memo line, at the bottom left of the check."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:54:51-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, right. Bottom left. Okay. Thank you, Miss Whitcomb. I'm still a little mixed up on the whole year, half year thing, but I'll look at it again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:55:01-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The installment amount is the one marked as due on the stub. Now, shall I transfer you to the Assessor's office?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:55:09-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes please. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T13:55:11-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One moment, please, while I connect you."
    }
  ],
